---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="White, grey and near-black" surface="none" padding="none" code={'<section class="section">…</section>\n<section class="section tone-alt">…</section>\n<section class="section tone-dark">…</section>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Pages are built from full-width bands. Alternating white and grey separates sections without lines; a near-black band marks a capstone moment and stays dark in light mode.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="bands">
        <div class="band"><p class="label">section</p><p class="band-title">The default band.</p><Button href="#white-grey-and-near-black" variant="link">Learn more</Button></div>
        <div class="band tone-alt"><p class="label">section tone-alt</p><p class="band-title">The grey band.</p><Button href="#white-grey-and-near-black" variant="link">Learn more</Button></div>
        <div class="band tone-dark"><p class="label">section tone-dark</p><p class="band-title">The near-black band. <span class="gradient-text">Always dark.</span></p><Button href="#white-grey-and-near-black" variant="link">Learn more</Button></div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Rhythm" surface="none">
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>A typical page: hero, white, grey, near-black for the capstone product, grey, then the closing call to action on white. Never two near-black bands in a row.</p></Fragment>
    <ol class="rhythm" role="list">
        <li class="r-hero">Hero</li>
        <li class="r-white">White</li>
        <li class="r-grey">Grey</li>
        <li class="r-dark">Near-black</li>
        <li class="r-grey">Grey</li>
        <li class="r-white">CTA</li>
    </ol>
</Specimen>

<style>
    .bands {
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    }

    .band {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        justify-items: start;
        padding: 3rem clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3rem);
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
    }

    .band.tone-alt {
        background: var(--bg-alt);
    }

    .band-title {
        color: var(--heading);
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-size: var(--text-3xl);
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    }

    .rhythm {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
        gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .rhythm li {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        height: 5rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }

    .r-hero { background: var(--brand-gradient); color: #fff; border: 0; }
    .r-white { background: var(--bg); }
    .r-grey { background: var(--bg-alt); }
    .r-dark { background: #000; color: #f5f5f7; }
</style>
